invariant: INV-16
file: hash_hw.h
catches: test/hash-builds.sh
reason: hash_hw.h no longer renames sha256_final, so the copies hkdf_hw.c and
  keysched_hw.c hold start each hash on the instructions and end it on
  sha256.c. Every digest is the same, because the two paths keep one
  state, so no vector fails; a session that stated the instructions runs
  a third of its hash calls on the portable code. The script reads the
  symbols each copy calls, for x86-64 and for arm64 under the pinned
  clang, and requires the three _hw names and none of sha256.c's.

--- old
#define sha256_final sha256_final_hw
--- new
